(5913072, 859533, 76712, '<td valign="top">well done for the new 4th place and green ribbon aha :)</td>', 'well done for the new 4th place and green ribbon aha :)', '2010-03-22 09:57:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(5913278, 858907, 105457, '<td valign="top">Hi Walter, greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>So you decided to take the plunge and enter in the challenges, and for the first entry you landed a 37th place, very good!<br/> <br/>Regarding your photo:<br/> <br/>Composition<br/>Although the tree in front does detract a bit from the image, the overall lines help to lessen this effect. Your eyes are attracted to the waves and a bit away from the trees, as if they are secondary.<br/> <br/>Technique / Lighting<br/>As mentioned below, with a shutter speed of 1/2000 you had some space to compromise in aperture and maybe a lower ISO (but I guess with minus 27 it was better not to have the picture shaken :)<br/> <br/>Processing<br/>Here is where I think it was a bit overdone. The levels and saturation caused that blue halo around the tree trunks, giving it a rather HDR feel to it (not in a good way). Probably you could have gone in the opposite direction, slightly desaturating it, and boosted the contrast, then you could''ve retained the original punch.<br/> <br/>Overall<br/>For this challenge this fitted perfectly, and you still got a 6.8 from commentators, so it pleased a lot of people.<br/>I think that this picture with good processing could easily be in the top 20.<br/> <br/>Continue sending in pictures :)<br/>PS - if you want (since you''re a member, you can do it) instead of putting your comments in the comment section, you can edit the details of the picture, and include it in the description.<br/> <br/>If you have any questions feel free to <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/messaging.php?action=compose&amp;USER_ID=105457" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">contact me</a>.<br/>Regards,<br/>Joao</td>', 'Hi Walter, greetings from the Critique Club! So you decided to take the plunge and enter in the challenges, and for the first entry you landed a 37th place, very good! Regarding your photo: CompositionAlthough the tree in front does detract a bit from the image, the overall lines help to lessen this effect. Your eyes are attracted to the waves and a bit away from the trees, as if they are secondary. Technique / LightingAs mentioned below, with a shutter speed of 1/2000 you had some space to compromise in aperture and maybe a lower ISO (but I guess with minus 27 it was better not to have the picture shaken :) ProcessingHere is where I think it was a bit overdone. The levels and saturation caused that blue halo around the tree trunks, giving it a rather HDR feel to it (not in a good way). Probably you could have gone in the opposite direction, slightly desaturating it, and boosted the contrast, then you could''ve retained the original punch. OverallFor this challenge this fitted perfectly, and you still got a 6.8 from commentators, so it pleased a lot of people.I think that this picture with good processing could easily be in the top 20. Continue sending in pictures :)PS - if you want (since you''re a member, you can do it) instead of putting your comments in the comment section, you can edit the details of the picture, and include it in the description. If you have any questions feel free to contact me.Regards,Joao', '2010-03-22 12:43:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(5913294, 859775, 105457, '<td valign="top">Hi Ronnie, greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Well, nothing much to say about this one, super congrats on your personal best and ribbon!<br/>Stunning shot, and yes, it''s straight :) I used the word "Romance" as a reference, and it''s not crooked.<br/> <br/>Great choice on the b&amp;w, great composition on not centering the subject, good balance between highlights and shadows. And 1/15s handheld?? Great job!<br/> <br/>If you have any questions feel free to <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/messaging.php?action=compose&amp;USER_ID=105457" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">contact me</a>.<br/>Regards,<br/>Joao<br/></td>', 'Hi Ronnie, greetings from the Critique Club! Well, nothing much to say about this one, super congrats on your personal best and ribbon!Stunning shot, and yes, it''s straight :) I used the word "Romance" as a reference, and it''s not crooked. Great choice on the b&w, great composition on not centering the subject, good balance between highlights and shadows. And 1/15s handheld?? Great job! If you have any questions feel free to contact me.Regards,Joao', '2010-03-22 13:02:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(5913407, 859673, 60495, '<td valign="top">It''s really fun to take a second look at images, this is one of those shots that have a lot of interest when you take the time to really look at it. First time I saw it I was not all that impressed but after taking a second look I love the way the flying shadow flows directly off the sitting bird. Nice capture!</td>', 'It''s really fun to take a second look at images, this is one of those shots that have a lot of interest when you take the time to really look at it. First time I saw it I was not all that impressed but after taking a second look I love the way the flying shadow flows directly off the sitting bird. Nice capture!', '2010-03-22 14:32:53.000000', NULL, 0),
