(5920022, 858991, 22734, '<td valign="top">This should have scored higher. Much stronger if the left arm was not showing so as to let eyes slide down the curls of hair with the beautiful neck contour.</td>', 'This should have scored higher. Much stronger if the left arm was not showing so as to let eyes slide down the curls of hair with the beautiful neck contour.', '2010-03-28 18:21:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(5922917, 859494, 50641, '<td valign="top">let''s see - by the current definition of the artwork rule:  you initially fooled us into believing he really has a shadow..?  very clever setup and you''re generous to share it.</td>', 'let''s see - by the current definition of the artwork rule:  you initially fooled us into believing he really has a shadow..?  very clever setup and you''re generous to share it.', '2010-03-31 01:39:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(5923628, 859494, 61396, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by skewsme:</b></div><hr/><i> let''s see - by the current definition of the artwork rule:  you initially fooled us into believing he really has a shadow..?  very clever setup and you''re generous to share it. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I didn''t initially intended to mess with the artwork rule. It was an accident and a surprise to me. The original idea was to interchange the roles of a real figure and its (unreal) shadow. I hoped to depict it here where the shadow is real and the figure is blatantly not. Also, I didn''t invent the technique (of back lighting the cardboard made shadow image), but used it after more obvious techniques miserably failed to work for me.</td>', 'Originally posted by skewsme: let''s see - by the current definition of the artwork rule:  you initially fooled us into believing he really has a shadow..?  very clever setup and you''re generous to share it.   I didn''t initially intended to mess with the artwork rule. It was an accident and a surprise to me. The original idea was to interchange the roles of a real figure and its (unreal) shadow. I hoped to depict it here where the shadow is real and the figure is blatantly not. Also, I didn''t invent the technique (of back lighting the cardboard made shadow image), but used it after more obvious techniques miserably failed to work for me.', '2010-03-31 14:15:24.000000', NULL, 0),
